# AI Provider Tycoon — Design Spec v0.1

## Concept

Multiplayer tycoon game where players compete to become the #1 AI provider. The only human input is a prompt, written and locked before the match. Each player is then represented by an LLM agent acting on that prompt. Humans watch the result unfold.

It's a prompt-engineering tournament wearing a tycoon costume.

## Core economic model

**Resources**
- Money (primary; bankruptcy = elimination)
- Servers (split between inference and research)
- Talent (research velocity multiplier)
- Models (research outputs; quality and recency drive demand)
- Brand / market awareness (marketing-derived; converts to demand)

**Levers**
- Invest in research
- Invest in marketing
- Allocate servers (inference vs. research)
- Hire / fire talent
- Buy or upgrade servers
- Pricing (implicit; may need to be explicit)

**Flows**
- Revenue = f(demand, hosting capacity, model quality, price)
- Demand = f(brand, model quality vs. competitors, price)
- New models = f(research compute, talent, time)
- Costs = servers + salaries + marketing spend + COGS

